---
/**
 * The three fixed layers behind the content: an atmosphere that lifts the top of the page
 * off pure black, the 120px rule grid, and a pair of very slow radial drifts. Nothing here
 * reads as an animation while you look at it - the movement is slower than attention.
 *
 * `.prog` is the scroll-progress bar; `.grid-bg` reads `--gridY`, which the page script
 * writes so the grid drifts at a fraction of the page's own speed.
 */
---

<div class="ground" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="drift a"></span>
  <span class="drift b"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div class="prog"></div>
